matchingFieldFromPermutation -- Matching field parametrised by permutations
***************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Lgr = matchingFieldFromPermutation(k, n, S)
        Lfl = matchingFieldFromPermutation(tupleSizeList, n, S)
  * Inputs:
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, positive integer; the size of
        the tuples of the Grassmannian matching field
      * tupleSizeList, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, positive integers;
        the sizes of the tuples of the flag matching field
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, positive integer; the tuples
        have entries in 1 .. n
      * S, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, permutation of 1 .. n
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * RowNum => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 2, which
        row of the digonal weight matrix to permute
      * UsePrimePowers => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value false, use multiples of prime power used for the entries
        of the diagonal weight matrix
      * PowerValue => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 0, use
        multiples of powers this value in the diagonal weight matrix
      * ScalingCoefficient => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default
        value 1, the value by which to scale the permuted row of the diagonal
        weight matrix
  * Outputs:
      * Lgr, an instance of the type *note GrMatchingField: GrMatchingField,, 
      * Lfl, an instance of the type *note FlMatchingField: FlMatchingField,, 

Description
===========

Let $M_0 \in \RR^{k \times n}$ be a matrix that induces the diagonal matching
field. Usually, we take this matrix to be $(m_{i,j})$ with $m_{i,j} =
(n-j)n^(i-2)$ if $i > 1$ and $m_{i,j} = 0$ if $i = 1$. Note that this matrix is
different to the weight matrix of the matching field produced by the function
*note diagonalMatchingField: diagonalMatchingField,, however the matching
fields are the same. Given a permutation $\sigma \in S_n$, the matching field
associated to $\sigma$ has weight matrix $M_\sigma$, which is the same as $M_0$
except for the second row. The second row of $M_\sigma$ is obtained from the
second row of $M$ by permuting the entries according to $\sigma$. Explicitly,
they are given by $\sigma(1), \sigma(2), \dots, \sigma(n)$. For instance, if
$\sigma = (n, n-1, \dots, 1) \in S_n$ is the permutation written in single-line
notation, then the matching field induced by $M_\sigma$ is the diagonal
matching field.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L0 = diagonalMatchingField(3, 6)                            |
|                                                                 |
|o1 = Grassmannian Matching Field for Gr(3, 6)                    |
|                                                                 |
|o1 : GrMatchingField                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : getWeightMatrix L0                                          |
|                                                                 |
|o2 = | 0  0  0 0 0 0 |                                           |
|     | 6  5  4 3 2 1 |                                           |
|     | 12 10 8 6 4 2 |                                           |
|                                                                 |
|              3       6                                          |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : L1 = matchingFieldFromPermutation(3, 6, {6,5,4,3,2,1})      |
|                                                                 |
|o3 = Grassmannian Matching Field for Gr(3, 6)                    |
|                                                                 |
|o3 : GrMatchingField                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : getWeightMatrix L1                                          |
|                                                                 |
|o4 = | 0  0  0  0  0 0 |                                         |
|     | 6  5  4  3  2 1 |                                         |
|     | 30 24 18 12 6 0 |                                         |
|                                                                 |
|              3       6                                          |
|o4 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : L0 == L1                                                    |
|                                                                 |
|o5 = true                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : L2 = matchingFieldFromPermutation(3, 6, {1,3,2,6,4,5})      |
|                                                                 |
|o6 = Grassmannian Matching Field for Gr(3, 6)                    |
|                                                                 |
|o6 : GrMatchingField                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : getWeightMatrix L2                                          |
|                                                                 |
|o7 = | 0  0  0  0  0 0 |                                         |
|     | 1  3  2  6  4 5 |                                         |
