UsePrimePowers -- Use a diagonal weight matrix with multiples of certain powers
*******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Lgr = matchingFieldFromPermutation(k, n, S, UsePrimePowers => b, PowerValue => v)
        Lfl = matchingFieldFromPermutation(tupleSizeList, n, S, UsePrimePowers => b, PowerValue => v)
  * Inputs:
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * tupleSizeList, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * S, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a permutation of $1, \dots, n$
      * r, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, set whether prime
        powers are to be used
      * v, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, set the value of the powers to
        be used
  * Outputs:
      * Lgr, an instance of the type *note GrMatchingField: GrMatchingField,, 
      * Lfl, an instance of the type *note FlMatchingField: FlMatchingField,, 

Description
===========

The options *note UsePrimePowers: UsePrimePowers, and *note PowerValue:
UsePrimePowers, are optional arguments for the function *note
matchingFieldFromPermutation: matchingFieldFromPermutation,, which constructs a
matching field by permuting a row (usually the second row) of a weight matrix
that gives rise to the diagonal matching field.

If the option *note UsePrimePowers: UsePrimePowers, is set to true, then the
underlying diagonal weight matrix is given by $M_0 = (m_{i,j})$ with $m_{i,j} =
(n-j) p^(i-2)$ if $i > 1$ and $m_{i,j} = 0$ if $i = 1$, where $p \ge n$ is the
smallest prime number greater than or equal to $n$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : getWeightMatrix matchingFieldFromPermutation(3, 6, {1,2,3,4,5,6},       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = | 0  0  0  0  0 0 |                                                     |
|     | 1  2  3  4  5 6 |                                                     |
|     | 30 24 18 12 6 0 |                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|              3       6                                                      |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|UsePrimePowers => false)                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : getWeightMatrix matchingFieldFromPermutation(3, 6, {1,2,3,4,5,6},       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = | 0  0  0  0  0 0 |                                                     |
|     | 1  2  3  4  5 6 |                                                     |
|     | 35 28 21 14 7 0 |                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|              3       6                                                      |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|UsePrimePowers => true)                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

To set the value of $p$ in the above matrix to a specific value, use the option
*note PowerValue: UsePrimePowers,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : getWeightMatrix matchingFieldFromPermutation(3, 6, {1,2,3,4,5,6},       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = | 0  0  0  0  0  0 |                                                    |
|     | 1  2  3  4  5  6 |                                                    |
|     | 50 40 30 20 10 0 |                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|              3       6                                                      |
|o3 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|PowerValue => 10)                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The option *note PowerValue: UsePrimePowers, overrides the option *note
UsePrimePowers: UsePrimePowers,.

Warning. Certain values for the option *note PowerValue: UsePrimePowers, will
produce weight matrices that are not generic, i.e., the initial term of the
corresponding Pluecker forms are not all monomials, hence the weight matrix
does not define a matching field. The function *note
matchingFieldFromPermutation: matchingFieldFromPermutation, will produce a
matching field, which may lead to unexpected behaviours.

Precise details. The value of $p$ is determined as follows. The option *note
PowerValue: UsePrimePowers, is used if it is a positive value. If *note
PowerValue: UsePrimePowers, is not positive then the function checks to see if
the option *note UsePrimePowers: UsePrimePowers, is set to true. If it is, then
the value of $p$ is set to be the small prime number greater than or equal to
$n$. Otherwise, if *note UsePrimePowers: UsePrimePowers, is set to false, then
$p$ is set to be $n$.

