ScalingCoefficient -- Scale the permuted row of the weight matrix
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Lgr = matchingFieldFromPermutation(k, n, S, ScalingCoefficient => c)
        Lfl = matchingFieldFromPermutation(tupleSizeList, n, S, ScalingCoefficient => c)
  * Inputs:
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * tupleSizeList, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * S, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a permutation of $1, \dots, n$
      * c, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, scale the value of permuted row
        by $c$
  * Outputs:
      * Lgr, an instance of the type *note GrMatchingField: GrMatchingField,, 
      * Lfl, an instance of the type *note FlMatchingField: FlMatchingField,, 

Description
===========

The function *note matchingFieldFromPermutation: matchingFieldFromPermutation,
constructs a weight matrix by permuting the row of a weight matrix that induces
the diagonal matching field. The option *note ScalingCoefficient:
ScalingCoefficient, sets the scaling coefficient of the row being permuted,
which by default is $1$.

Note that by setting the option *note UsePrimePowers: UsePrimePowers, to true,
it guarantees that the weight matrix is generic, i.e., the matching field is
well defined, as long as the scaling coefficient is less than the prime power
used.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
