getTuples -- The tuples of a matching field
*******************************************

  * Usage: 
        tuples = getTuples L
  * Inputs:
      * L, an instance of the type *note MatchingField: MatchingField,, an
        instance of the type *note GrMatchingField: GrMatchingField,, or an
        instance of the type *note FlMatchingField: FlMatchingField,,
  * Outputs:
      * tuples, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, A list of subsets of $1,
        \dots, n$; the tuples of the matching field

Description
===========

A matching field $\Lambda$ for the Grassmannian Gr$(k, n)$ is a collection
tuples $\Lambda(J)$ for each $k$-subset $J \subseteq [n]$. The entries of the
tuple form a permutation of $J$, so in some literature $\Lambda(J)$ is taken to
be the element of the symmetric group $\sigma \in S_k$ such that $\Lambda(J) =
(j_{\sigma(1)}, j_{\sigma(2), \dots, j_{\sigma(k)}})$ where $J = \{j_1 < j_2 <
\dots < j_k\}$.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = diagonalMatchingField(2, 4)                 |
|                                                     |
|o1 = Grassmannian Matching Field for Gr(2, 4)        |
|                                                     |
|o1 : GrMatchingField                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : getTuples L                                     |
|                                                     |
|o2 = {{1, 2}, {1, 3}, {2, 3}, {1, 4}, {2, 4}, {3, 4}}|
|                                                     |
|o2 : List                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

The tuples are stored such that their underlying sets are in RevLex order,
which is the order produced by the method *note subsets:
(Macaulay2Doc)subsets,.

For flag matching fields, the tuples are stored as a list of list of tuples for
each Grassmannian matching field contained within.

+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : L = diagonalMatchingField({1,2}, 4)|
|                                        |
|o3 = Flag Matching Field for Fl(1, 2; 4)|
|                                        |
|o3 : FlMatchingField                    |
