getWeightMatrix -- weight matrix that induces the matching field
****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = getWeightMatrix L
  * Inputs:
      * L, an instance of the type *note MatchingField: MatchingField,, an
        instance of the type *note GrMatchingField: GrMatchingField,, or an
        instance of the type *note FlMatchingField: FlMatchingField,,
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, weight matrix that induces
        the matching field

Description
===========

If the supplied matching field is coherent, then this function returns a weight
matrix that induces the matching field. If the matching field was originally
defined by a weight matrix then that weight matrix is returned. Otherwise, a
weight matrix is computed. The weight matrix is computed by computing the
weight matrix cone, which can be returned with the function *note
weightMatrixCone: weightMatrixCone,. If the supplied matching field is not
coherent, then the function gives an error.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = diagonalMatchingField(2, 4)                                      |
|                                                                          |
|o1 = Grassmannian Matching Field for Gr(2, 4)                             |
|                                                                          |
|o1 : GrMatchingField                                                      |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : getWeightMatrix L                                                    |
|                                                                          |
|o2 = | 0 0 0 0 |                                                          |
|     | 4 3 2 1 |                                                          |
|                                                                          |
|              2       4                                                   |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : L = grMatchingField(2, 4, {{1,2}, {1,3}, {3,2}, {1,4}, {4,2}, {3,4}})|
|                                                                          |
|o3 = Grassmannian Matching Field for Gr(2, 4)                             |
|                                                                          |
|o3 : GrMatchingField                                                      |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isCoherent L                                                         |
|                                                                          |
|o4 = true                                                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : getWeightMatrix L                                                    |
|                                                                          |
|o5 = | 0 0  0  0  |                                                       |
|     | 0 -3 -1 -2 |                                                       |
|                                                                          |
|              2       4                                                   |
|o5 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The weight on the ring containing the Pluecker forms, i.e., minors of a generic
matrix, is based on the weight matrix returned by *note getWeightMatrix:
getWeightMatrix,. Note that the package *note MatchingFields: Top, uses the
minimum convention but polynomial ring weight vectors use the maximum
convention so some conversion is required.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : plueckerMap L                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = map (QQ[x   ..x   ], QQ[p   ..p   , p   , p   , p   , p   ], {x   x    -|
|              1,1   2,4       1,2   1,3   2,3   1,4   2,4   3,4     1,1 2,2  |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : RingMap QQ[x   ..x   ] <-- QQ[p   ..p   , p   , p   , p   , p   ]       |
|                 1,1   2,4          1,2   1,3   2,3   1,4   2,4   3,4        |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x   x   , x   x    - x   x   , - x   x    + x   x   , x   x    - x   x   , - |
| 1,2 2,1   1,1 2,3    1,3 2,1     1,3 2,2    1,2 2,3   1,1 2,4    1,4 2,1    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x   x    + x   x   , x   x    - x   x   })                                   |
| 1,4 2,2    1,2 2,4   1,3 2,4    1,4 2,3                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : R = target plueckerMap L                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : describe R                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = QQ[x   ..x   , Degrees => {8:1}, Heft => {1}, MonomialOrder =>          |
|         1,1   2,4                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{MonomialSize => 32       }]                                                 |
|{Weights => {5:0, 3, 1..2}}                                                  |
|{GRevLex => {8:1}         }                                                  |
|{Position => Up           }                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note getWeightPluecker: getWeightPluecker, -- weight of the Pluecker
    variables induced by the weight matrix
  * *note plueckerMap: plueckerMap, -- The ring map of the Pluecker embedding
  * *note weightMatrixCone: weightMatrixCone, -- The cone of weight matrices
    that induce the matching field
* Menu:


