plueckerMap -- The ring map of the Pluecker embedding
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        m = plueckerMap L
  * Inputs:
      * L, an instance of the type *note MatchingField: MatchingField,, an
        instance of the type *note GrMatchingField: GrMatchingField,, or an
        instance of the type *note FlMatchingField: FlMatchingField,,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * MonomialOrder => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value
        "default", either "default" or "none" (supply "none" only if $L$ is not
        coherent)
  * Outputs:
      * m, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, the ring map of the
        Pluecker embedding

Description
===========

The ring map for the Pluecker embedding of the Grassmannian sends each Pluecker
variable $P_J$, where $J$ is a $k$-subset of $[n]$, to its corresponding
maximal minor in a generic $k \times n$ matrix of variables $X = (x_{i,j})$.

The domain and codomain of this ring map are naturally equipped with term
orders derived from a weight matrix, which induces the matching field. So, for
this function, we require that the matching fields be coherent. If a weight
matrix is not supplied, then one is automatically computed. If the matching
field is not coherent, then an error is thrown.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = grMatchingField(2, 4, {{1, 2}, {1, 3}, {3, 2}, {1, 4}, {4, 2}, {3,  |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = Grassmannian Matching Field for Gr(2, 4)                                |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : GrMatchingField                                                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|4}})                                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isCoherent L                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : getWeightMatrix L                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = | 0 0  0  0  |                                                          |
|     | 0 -3 -1 -2 |                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|              2       4                                                      |
|o3 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : plueckerMap L                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = map (QQ[x   ..x   ], QQ[p   ..p   , p   , p   , p   , p   ], {x   x    -|
|              1,1   2,4       1,2   1,3   2,3   1,4   2,4   3,4     1,1 2,2  |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : RingMap QQ[x   ..x   ] <-- QQ[p   ..p   , p   , p   , p   , p   ]       |
|                 1,1   2,4          1,2   1,3   2,3   1,4   2,4   3,4        |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x   x   , x   x    - x   x   , - x   x    + x   x   , x   x    - x   x   , - |
| 1,2 2,1   1,1 2,3    1,3 2,1     1,3 2,2    1,2 2,3   1,1 2,4    1,4 2,1    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x   x    + x   x   , x   x    - x   x   })                                   |
| 1,4 2,2    1,2 2,4   1,3 2,4    1,4 2,3                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : describe target plueckerMap L                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = QQ[x   ..x   , Degrees => {8:1}, Heft => {1}, MonomialOrder =>          |
|         1,1   2,4                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{MonomialSize => 32       }]                                                 |
|{Weights => {5:0, 3, 1..2}}                                                  |
|{GRevLex => {8:1}         }                                                  |
|{Position => Up           }                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

For the above polynomial ring, the monomial order is given by a weight
ordering. Note that the weights are based on $-1 \times W$ where $W$ is the
weight matrix that induces $L$, displayed using the function *note
getWeightMatrix: getWeightMatrix,. The purpose of $-1$ is to transition between
the minimum convention of matching fields and the maximum convention of initial
terms in *note Macaulay2: (Macaulay2Doc)Top,.

The ring map for the Pluecker embedding of a partial flag variety is completely
analogous.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : L = diagonalMatchingField({1,2}, 4)                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = Flag Matching Field for Fl(1, 2; 4)                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : FlMatchingField                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : getWeightMatrix L                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = | 0 0 0 0 |                                                             |
|     | 4 3 2 1 |                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|              2       4                                                      |
|o7 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : m = plueckerMap L                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = map (QQ[x   ..x   ], QQ[p ..p , p   ..p   , p   , p   , p   ,           |
|              1,1   2,4       1   4   1,2   1,3   2,3   1,4   2,4            |
|                                                                             |
|o8 : RingMap QQ[x   ..x   ] <-- QQ[p ..p , p   ..p   , p   , p   ,           |
|                 1,1   2,4          1   4   1,2   1,3   2,3   1,4            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|p   ], {x   , x   , x   , x   , x   x    - x   x   , x   x    - x   x   ,    |
| 3,4     1,1   1,2   1,3   1,4   1,1 2,2    1,2 2,1   1,1 2,3    1,3 2,1     |
|                                                                             |
|p   , p   ]                                                                  |
| 2,4   3,4                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x   x    - x   x   , x   x    - x   x   , x   x    - x   x   , x   x    -    |
| 1,2 2,3    1,3 2,2   1,1 2,4    1,4 2,1   1,2 2,4    1,4 2,2   1,3 2,4      |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x   x   })                                                                   |
| 1,4 2,3                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : describe source m                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = QQ[p ..p , p   ..p   , p   , p   , p   , p   , Degrees => {10:1}, Heft  |
|         1   4   1,2   1,3   2,3   1,4   2,4   3,4                           |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|=> {1}, MonomialOrder => {MonomialSize => 32               }]                |
|                         {Weights => {4:3, 0..1, 1..2, 2:2}}                 |
|                         {GRevLex => {10:1}                }                 |
|                         {Position => Up                   }                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The monomial order on the ring of Pluecker variables, shown above, is also
based on $-1 \times W$. More concretely, the weight vector of a Pluecker
variable $P_J$ is the weight of the initial term of the image of the Pluecker
variable $m(P_J) = \det(X_J)$ under the map.

The monomial map associated to the matching field, see *note
matchingFieldRingMap: matchingFieldRingMap, is the map that sends each Pluecker
variable $P_J \mapsto \rm{in}(\det(X_J))$ to the lead term of the maximal minor
$\det(X_J)$.

