isLinkage -- Test if a tope field is linkage
********************************************

  * Usage: 
        result = isLinkage MF
        result = isLinkage TF
  * Inputs:
      * MF, an instance of the type *note GrMatchingField: GrMatchingField,, 
      * TF, an instance of the type *note TopeField: TopeField,, 
  * Outputs:
      * result, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Consider a tope field given by a collection of bipartite graphs. The tope field
is said to be linkage if for each $k+1$-subset $S$ of $[n]$, the union of the
edges of the bipartite graphs $G$ where the non-isolated left-vertices of $G$
are contained in $S$, is a forest. Note that all coherent matching fields are
linkage.

+------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = diagonalMatchingField(2,4);|
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : isLinkage L                    |
|                                    |
|o2 = true                           |
+------------------------------------+

